EmuSuNi's patch of DolphinPS4's Mesa winsys, port/mesa/ac_ps4_drm.c at DolphinPS4 720f60a (MIT, as the file):
scripts/setup.sh applies it after the DolphinPS4 checkout (DolphinPS4's build-mesa.sh copies the file into Mesa).
- The submissions' numbers, ac_ps4_get_submit_stats (the app's "gpu:" lines; the app needs it to link).
- The submission thread, off by default (an empty /data/EmuSuNi/gpu-submitthread-on turns it on): the kernel's
  calls (sceGnmSubmitCommandBuffers, ...AndFlip..., sceGnmSubmitDone) made in sequence order on a thread of its own,
  not on the thread that submits; written for EmuSuNi from the idea of Crema's winsys (read, not copied).
- (01.87) The IB-chain check's sceKernelVirtualQuery remembered per mapping until the winsys unmaps anything
  (gpu-ibcheckcache-on, off by default), and the buffers' tail check timed and, with gpu-lighttails-on (off by
  default), spread over the submissions and lighter.
